From 4babf2b408e711e77bea246196498eee816df4a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGNative <luis@nativestride.io>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 15:52:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/26] Theme: uniform dark logo chips with auto-inverted mono
 marks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every ticker logo now sits on one uniform dark chip in both light and dark
mode. Near-monochrome dark marks (measured per-logo from pixel luminance and
saturation — no per-asset table) are inverted so they read on the chip;
colourful logos keep their real colours. Treemap tiles in dark mode go from
0.45 to 0.85 opacity so gain/loss colours stay vivid. Solana logo replaced
with the real mark (+ SOL-EUR variant); stray SOL copy.png removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
